('ramayana-1-44-23', 'en', 'This is why gods are ''suras'' and demons ''asuras''.', 'A playful old explanation of the words sura and asura.', '[{"word":"sura","meaning":"god (lit. with wine)"},{"word":"asura","meaning":"demon (lit. without wine)"}]'::jsonb, 'veda-app-ai-draft', 'draft'),
('ramayana-1-44-24', 'en', 'The divine horse, jewel and nectar emerged.', 'Bala Kanda, chapter 44: they cross the Ganga to Vishala, and Vishvamitra tells of the churning of the ocean.', '[{"word":"uccaiḥśravas","meaning":"divine horse"},{"word":"kaustubha","meaning":"jewel"},{"word":"amṛta","meaning":"nectar"}]'::jsonb, 'veda-app-ai-draft', 'draft'),
('ramayana-1-44-25', 'en', 'They fought over the nectar.', 'Bala Kanda, chapter 44: they cross the Ganga to Vishala, and Vishvamitra tells of the churning of the ocean.', '[{"word":"kulakṣaya","meaning":"destruction of the family"}]'::jsonb, 'veda-app-ai-draft', 'draft'),
