('ramayana-2-56-3', 'en', 'Two griefs burn him at once.', 'Ayodhya Kanda, chapter 56: Dasharatha folds his hands and asks Kausalya''s forgiveness. She is moved, apologises in turn, and explains that grief made her speak harshly. Her lines on how grief destroys everything are among the best known in the epic. The idea of the husband as a god reflects the values of the age and is best read in that historical context.', '[{"word":"dahyamāna","meaning":"burning"},{"word":"bhūpati","meaning":"king"},{"word":"amanas","meaning":"dejected"}]'::jsonb, 'veda-app-ai-draft', 'draft'),
