('ramayana-2-57-1', 'en', 'The king wakes and broods.', 'Ayodhya Kanda, chapter 57: On the sixth night after Rama left, Dasharatha remembers a sin of his youth. As a prince proud of hitting targets by sound alone, he shot an arrow into the dark by the Sarayu river and struck a young ascetic filling a water pot. He now sees his present grief as the fruit of that act.', '[{"word":"pratibuddha","meaning":"awakened"},{"word":"cintā","meaning":"anxious thought"},{"word":"śokopahata","meaning":"struck by grief"}]'::jsonb, 'veda-app-ai-draft', 'draft'),
