('ramayana-2-57-22', 'en', 'A senseless act of harm is condemned by all.', 'Ayodhya Kanda, chapter 57: On the sixth night after Rama left, Dasharatha remembers a sin of his youth. As a prince proud of hitting targets by sound alone, he shot an arrow into the dark by the Sarayu river and struck a young ascetic filling a water pot. He now sees his present grief as the fruit of that act.', '[{"word":"niṣphala","meaning":"fruitless"},{"word":"anartha","meaning":"harm"},{"word":"gurutalpaga","meaning":"one who violates his teacher''s bed"}]'::jsonb, 'veda-app-ai-draft', 'draft'),
('ramayana-2-57-23', 'en', 'The dying youth thinks first of his helpless parents.', 'Ayodhya Kanda, chapter 57: Dasharatha tells Kausalya how, as a young prince, he shot at a sound in the dark by the Sarayu and mortally wounded a young ascetic who was fetching water for his blind, aged parents. The dying youth asks him to go to his father and to draw out the arrow.', '[{"word":"jīvitakṣaya","meaning":"end of life"},{"word":"anuśocāmi","meaning":"I grieve for"},{"word":"mātṛ","meaning":"mother"}]'::jsonb, 'veda-app-ai-draft', 'draft'),
