('ramayana-2-57-35', 'en', 'Even dying, he tries to protect his killer.', 'Ayodhya Kanda, chapter 57: Dasharatha tells Kausalya how, as a young prince, he shot at a sound in the dark by the Sarayu and mortally wounded a young ascetic who was fetching water for his blind, aged parents. The dying youth asks him to go to his father and to draw out the arrow.', '[{"word":"ekapadī","meaning":"footpath"},{"word":"āśrama","meaning":"hermitage"},{"word":"śapet","meaning":"may curse"}]'::jsonb, 'veda-app-ai-draft', 'draft'),
('ramayana-2-57-36', 'en', 'He asks for the arrow to be removed.', 'Ayodhya Kanda, chapter 57: Dasharatha tells Kausalya how, as a young prince, he shot at a sound in the dark by the Sarayu and mortally wounded a young ascetic who was fetching water for his blind, aged parents. The dying youth asks him to go to his father and to draw out the arrow. The youth''s words about his birth reflect the caste ideas of the time: killing a Brahmin was held the gravest sin, and he reassures the prince he is not one.', '[{"word":"viśalya","meaning":"free of the arrow"},{"word":"śara","meaning":"arrow"},{"word":"ambu","meaning":"water"}]'::jsonb, 'veda-app-ai-draft', 'draft'),
('ramayana-2-57-37', 'en', 'He tries to ease the prince''s guilt. The caste labels reflect ancient social categories, not anyone''s worth.', 'Ayodhya Kanda, chapter 57: Dasharatha tells Kausalya how, as a young prince, he shot at a sound in the dark by the Sarayu and mortally wounded a young ascetic who was fetching water for his blind, aged parents. The dying youth asks him to go to his father and to draw out the arrow. The youth''s words about his birth reflect the caste ideas of the time: killing a Brahmin was held the gravest sin, and he reassures the prince he is not one. The moral weight of the story does not depend on this.', '[{"word":"dvijāti","meaning":"twice-born"},{"word":"vaiśya","meaning":"Vaishya"},{"word":"śūdrā","meaning":"Shudra woman"}]'::jsonb, 'veda-app-ai-draft', 'draft'),
