('ramayana-2-61-1', 'en', 'The leaders meet to decide what to do.', 'Ayodhya Kanda, chapter 61: The next morning the sages and ministers gather. They describe, verse by verse, the chaos that befalls a land without a ruler, and urge Vasishtha to install a prince as king at once. The passage is a classic Indian reflection on why order and just government matter.', '[{"word":"rājakartṛ","meaning":"king-maker"},{"word":"sabhā","meaning":"assembly"},{"word":"udaya","meaning":"rising"}]'::jsonb, 'veda-app-ai-draft', 'draft'),
