('ramayana-2-68-1', 'en', 'He continues his rebuke.', 'Ayodhya Kanda, chapter 68: Bharata''s anger continues. He tells the story of Surabhi, the divine mother of cows, who wept to see her sons the oxen suffering under the plough, to show how deep a mother''s love is and how Kaikeyi has wounded Kausalya. He vows to bring Rama back. His harsh words are the outburst of a grieving son and are not presented as the epic''s last word on Kaikeyi.', '[{"word":"garhayitvā","meaning":"having reproached"},{"word":"roṣa","meaning":"anger"},{"word":"āviṣṭa","meaning":"filled"}]'::jsonb, 'veda-app-ai-draft', 'draft'),
