('ramayana-2-68-28', 'en', 'He collapses in anger and grief.', 'Ayodhya Kanda, chapter 68: Bharata''s anger continues. He tells the story of Surabhi, the divine mother of cows, who wept to see her sons the oxen suffering under the plough, to show how deep a mother''s love is and how Kaikeyi has wounded Kausalya. He vows to bring Rama back. His harsh words are the outburst of a grieving son and are not presented as the epic''s last word on Kaikeyi.', '[{"word":"tomara","meaning":"lance"},{"word":"aṅkuśa","meaning":"elephant hook"},{"word":"pannaga","meaning":"snake"}]'::jsonb, 'veda-app-ai-draft', 'draft'),
