('ramayana-2-69-1', 'en', 'Kausalya hears Bharata''s cries.', 'Ayodhya Kanda, chapter 69: Kausalya, suspecting Bharata had a hand in the exile, speaks bitterly to him. Bharata answers with a long series of oaths: may whoever approved of Rama''s exile bear the guilt of every kind of wrongdoing. The list is a window into the moral code of the time. Kausalya is convinced of his innocence and embraces him.', '[{"word":"krośat","meaning":"crying out"},{"word":"ājñāya","meaning":"hearing"},{"word":"sumitrā","meaning":"Sumitra"}]'::jsonb, 'veda-app-ai-draft', 'draft'),
