('ramayana-2-69-3', 'en', 'She goes to him in her grief.', 'Ayodhya Kanda, chapter 69: Kausalya, suspecting Bharata had a hand in the exile, speaks bitterly to him. Bharata answers with a long series of oaths: may whoever approved of Rama''s exile bear the guilt of every kind of wrongdoing. The list is a window into the moral code of the time. Kausalya is convinced of his innocence and embraces him.', '[{"word":"vivarṇa","meaning":"pale"},{"word":"malināmbara","meaning":"in soiled clothes"},{"word":"vepamāna","meaning":"trembling"}]'::jsonb, 'veda-app-ai-draft', 'draft'),
