('ramayana-2-94-1', 'en', 'Rama welcomes Bharata tenderly.', 'Ayodhya Kanda, chapter 94: Rama lifts Bharata, asks why he has come, and then asks him a long series of questions about how he is governing. This ''Kaccit'' chapter (''I hope that...'') is a classic Indian guide to good kingship: choosing wise ministers, keeping counsel, paying soldiers on time, caring for farmers and traders, and treating all fairly.', '[{"word":"āghrāya","meaning":"kissing"},{"word":"aṅka","meaning":"lap"},{"word":"samāhita","meaning":"attentive"}]'::jsonb, 'veda-app-ai-draft', 'draft'),
