('ramayana-2-95-1', 'en', 'Bharata feels unfit to rule.', 'Ayodhya Kanda, chapter 95: Bharata tells Rama that their father has died. Rama falls to the ground in grief. He then goes to the Mandakini with his brothers and Sita and offers water and a simple meal of ingudi paste to his father, saying that what a person eats is what his gods eat. The army and people, hearing their weeping, rush to the hermitage.', '[{"word":"rājadharma","meaning":"duty of kings"},{"word":"vihīna","meaning":"cut off"},{"word":"kariṣyati","meaning":"will do"}]'::jsonb, 'veda-app-ai-draft', 'draft'),
