('ramayana-2-98-1', 'en', 'A night of mourning passes.', 'Ayodhya Kanda, chapter 98: Bharata again offers the kingdom. Rama replies with one of the epic''s great reflections on life: all that gathers must scatter, all that rises must fall, every meeting ends in parting, and every life in death. Grieving cannot change this, so one should live rightly and keep one''s word. Bharata praises Rama''s steadiness and asks him to undo what their father did in confusion.', '[{"word":"rajanī","meaning":"night"},{"word":"suhṛdgaṇa","meaning":"friends"},{"word":"vyatyavartata","meaning":"passed"}]'::jsonb, 'veda-app-ai-draft', 'draft'),
