('ramayana-2-101-1', 'en', 'Rama answers Jabali.', 'Ayodhya Kanda, chapter 101: Rama firmly rejects Jabali''s argument. Character, not birth, shows who a person is; truth is the root of dharma and of the world; a king''s conduct shapes his people''s. He will not break his word. This chapter is one of the Ramayana''s great statements on truthfulness.', '[{"word":"yukti","meaning":"reasoning"},{"word":"avipanna","meaning":"unshaken"},{"word":"satyātman","meaning":"truthful"}]'::jsonb, 'veda-app-ai-draft', 'draft'),
