('ramayana-2-110-1', 'en', 'Sita replies.', 'Ayodhya Kanda, chapter 110: Sita replies that she knows a wife''s duty, and praises Rama''s goodness and respect toward all women. Pleased, Anasuya gives her divine garments, ornaments and an ever-fresh ointment, then asks to hear the story of her marriage. Sita tells how Janaka found her in a ploughed field, how no king could lift Shiva''s bow, and how Rama broke it and won her. The ideals of wifely service here are of their time; the warmth between the two women is timeless.', '[{"word":"asūyā","meaning":"envy"},{"word":"pratipūjya","meaning":"honouring"},{"word":"mandam","meaning":"softly"}]'::jsonb, 'veda-app-ai-draft', 'draft'),
