('ramayana-2-111-17', 'en', 'They prepare to move on.', 'Ayodhya Kanda, chapter 111: Anasuya embraces Sita, delighted with her story, and sends her back to Rama adorned in the divine gifts as night falls. The next morning the sages tell Rama of the dangerous, rakshasa-haunted forest ahead, and Rama, Sita and Lakshmana enter it, ending the Ayodhya Kanda.', '[{"word":"vyatīta","meaning":"passed"},{"word":"hutāgnika","meaning":"having made fire offerings"},{"word":"āpṛcchetām","meaning":"they took leave"}]'::jsonb, 'veda-app-ai-draft', 'draft'),
('ramayana-2-111-18', 'en', 'They are warned of danger ahead.', 'Ayodhya Kanda, chapter 111: Anasuya embraces Sita, delighted with her story, and sends her back to Rama adorned in the divine gifts as night falls. The next morning the sages tell Rama of the dangerous, rakshasa-haunted forest ahead, and Rama, Sita and Lakshmana enter it, ending the Ayodhya Kanda.', '[{"word":"vanacara","meaning":"forest dweller"},{"word":"saṃcāra","meaning":"path"},{"word":"samabhipluta","meaning":"overrun"}]'::jsonb, 'veda-app-ai-draft', 'draft'),
('ramayana-2-111-19', 'en', 'The sages show them the way.', 'Ayodhya Kanda, chapter 111: Anasuya embraces Sita, delighted with her story, and sends her back to Rama adorned in the divine gifts as night falls. The next morning the sages tell Rama of the dangerous, rakshasa-haunted forest ahead, and Rama, Sita and Lakshmana enter it, ending the Ayodhya Kanda.', '[{"word":"panthā","meaning":"path"},{"word":"āharatām","meaning":"gathering"},{"word":"durga","meaning":"hard to enter"}]'::jsonb, 'veda-app-ai-draft', 'draft'),
('ramayana-2-111-20', 'en', 'Rama, Sita and Lakshmana enter the deep forest, ending the Ayodhya Kanda.', 'Ayodhya Kanda, chapter 111: Anasuya embraces Sita, delighted with her story, and sends her back to Rama adorned in the divine gifts as night falls. The next morning the sages tell Rama of the dangerous, rakshasa-haunted forest ahead, and Rama, Sita and Lakshmana enter it, ending the Ayodhya Kanda.', '[{"word":"svastyayana","meaning":"blessing"},{"word":"sabhārya","meaning":"with his wife"},{"word":"abhramaṇḍala","meaning":"bank of clouds"}]'::jsonb, 'veda-app-ai-draft', 'draft');

