('ramayana-3-13-30', 'en', 'A traditional image of society as one body.', 'Aranya Kanda, chapter 13: on the way to Panchavati, Rama meets the great vulture Jatayu, his father''s friend, who tells of the origin of all creatures and offers to guard Sita. This echoes the Rig Veda''s Purusha hymn. Read today, the image is best understood as all people forming one body, not as ranking human worth.', '[{"word":"varna","meaning":"social class"},{"word":"shruti","meaning":"scripture"}]'::jsonb, 'veda-app-ai-draft', 'draft'),
