('ramayana-5-1-6', 'en', 'Hanuman on the slope.', 'Sundara Kanda, chapter 1: Hanuman leaps from Mount Mahendra across the ocean towards Lanka, and the Ocean asks Mount Mainaka to rise and give him a resting place.', '[{"word":"nāgavara","meaning":"great elephant"},{"word":"hrada","meaning":"lake"},{"word":"ābabhau","meaning":"looked like"}]'::jsonb, 'veda-app-ai-draft', 'draft'),
('ramayana-5-1-7', 'en', 'He prays before setting out.', 'Sundara Kanda, chapter 1: Hanuman leaps from Mount Mahendra across the ocean towards Lanka, and the Ocean asks Mount Mainaka to rise and give him a resting place. Hanuman''s prayer before a great task is a model of humility with strength.', '[{"word":"añjali","meaning":"folded hands"},{"word":"svayambhū","meaning":"self-born Brahma"},{"word":"mati","meaning":"resolve"}]'::jsonb, 'veda-app-ai-draft', 'draft'),
